{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he had possessions of flocks and possessions of cattle and a great household</b> — donkeys and camels and he-asses and slaves and maidservants. And Scripture mentions this but does not mention silver and gold as it said concerning Abraham (Genesis 13:2), because the greatness wherewith he grew great in the land of the Philistines was in livestock and household, and the Philistines envied him on that account. And this is the meaning of \"for you have become far too mighty for us\" — he said to him, even I, the king, have no livestock and household like yours, and it is a disgrace for us that your household should be greater than the king's household."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:24.319141784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}